{title: O Come All Ye Faithful}
{subtitle: Adeste Fideles}
{artist: John Francis Wade}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}
{tags: Christmas, Worship, Traditional, Hymn}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{comment: Triumphant and joyful - can be sung in Latin}

{start_of_verse}
O [G]come, all ye [D]faithful,
[G]Joyful and trium[D]phant,
O [Em]come ye, O [D]come ye, to [D]Beth[A]le[D]hem.
[G]Come and behold Him,
[Em]Born the King of [D]angels;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]O come, let us adore Him,
[G]O come, let us adore [D]Him,
[C]O come, let us ad[D]ore [Em]Him,
[C]Chri[D]st the [G]Lord.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Sing, choirs of [D]angels,
[G]Sing in exultat[D]ion;
O [Em]sing, all ye [D]citizens of [D]hea[A]ven ab[D]ove!
[G]Glory to God,
[Em]Glory in the [D]highest;
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Yea, Lord, we [D]greet Thee,
[G]Born this happy [D]morning;
[Em]Jesus, to [D]Thee be [D]glo[A]ry [D]given.
[G]Word of the Father,
[Em]Now in flesh ap[D]pearing;
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
